m Pietermaritzburg to Durban over 89.900 km. The race was held on Saturday, 31 May. Conditions: Cold at start, warming to mild late morning with clouds mid afternoon. Runners had 11 hours to complete the course.\n\nAlan ROBB claimed the men's title in 05:38:25, ahead of Bruce Foryce (05:40:31) and Malcolm Ball (05:40:45). Isavel ROCHE-KELLY won the women's race in 07:18:00, followed by Cheryl WINN (07:22:00).\n\nIsavel ROCHE-KELLY set a new women's course record of 07:18:00, surpassing Jan MALLEN's 08:22:41 from 1979. Women's runner-up Cheryl WINN's 07:22:00 also beat the previous women's record. Isavel ROCHE-KELLY's 07:18:00 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1932 (Bill Savage, 07:41:58).\n\nFrom a field of 3,979 entries, 3,977 runners completed the course for a 99.9% finish rate. The field comprised 3,941 men and 36 women (0.9% female). The average finish time was 08:58:05.\n\nMedals awarded: 10 Gold, 616 Silver, 3,351 Bronze. 1,678 runners (42.2%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Martin MANS in 10:59:00.\n\nCompared to the previous down run in 1978, the field was 53.0% larger.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 21% of the finishers, with 3,158 seniors (avg 08:56:33) and 817 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":0.1}